{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTowerBasicConstruction","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductiveCyclicity","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovCosetLift","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.spanning_shape_holds_for_identity_inclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.spanning_shape_holds_for_identity_inclusion","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L311-L327","doc":"**The spanning shape does NOT force a proper tower.** With `ιlow` the\nidentity, every `w` splits trivially — take `a := w` and an empty sum.\n\nSo `HeckeCosetSpanning` is consistent (it has a degenerate model, which is what\nmakes results conditional on it non-vacuous), and it is also *weaker than a\nproper inclusion*: an instance of it carries no information that `Hlow` is a\nstrict subalgebra. Anything needing properness must say so separately.\n\nStated over a bare `Ring` because the Hecke presentation binders carry no force\nhere — the observation is about the shape of the decomposition, not about\nHecke. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.hCE_fails_without_conditional_expectation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.hCE_fails_without_conditional_expectation","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L296-L309","doc":"**The `hCE` identity FAILS for a retraction that is not a conditional\nexpectation.** With `Hn = Hn1 = R = ℚ`, `ι = id` and `ε` = scaling by 2, the\nleft side is `2ax` and the right is `4ax`; at `a = x = 1` that reads `2 = 4`.\n\nSo `towerTrace_mul_eq_of_memB` genuinely consumes its instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.scaleTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.scaleTwo","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L291-L294","doc":"`ε` = \"scale by 2\" on `ℚ`: `ℚ`-linear, but neither a retraction of the\nidentity inclusion nor an `(Hn, Hn)`-bimodule map, so every field of\n`HeckeConditionalExpectation` fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.gwg_trace_towerE_of_spanning","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.gwg_trace_towerE_of_spanning","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L243-L272","doc":"**`hgwg` in the shape `cyclic_two_g` wants, for an arbitrary `w`.**\n`gwg_trace_of_spanning` exhibits the expectation as a decomposition sum;\n`towerE_eq_of_spanning` identifies that sum with `ι (ε w)`. Composing them gives\nthe reduction stated against `towerE` itself, with no residual `∃`.\n\nConditional on BOTH `HeckeCosetSpanning` and `HeckeMarkovExpectation`, neither\nof which has an instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.towerE_eq_of_spanning","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.towerE_eq_of_spanning","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L219-L241","doc":"**`ε` computed on an arbitrary element.** Spanning gives the decomposition;\nthe Markov property evaluates `ε` on each piece. Together they determine\n`ι (ε w)` outright:\n\n  `ιlow (εlow w) = ιlow a + Σᵢ z • (ιlow (b i) · ιlow (c i))`\n\nwhich is precisely the expectation `gwg_trace_of_spanning` exhibits. This is the\ncomposition the two classes exist to enable — neither alone says what `ε` does\nto a general element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.gwg_trace_of_spanning","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.gwg_trace_of_spanning","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L178-L217","doc":"**The `hgwg` reduction for an arbitrary `w`.** Given the spanning\ndecomposition and the two grounding shape lemmas — one for the lower-coset\nsummand, one for the middle — the two-generator Markov reduction holds for\nEVERY `w : Hn`.\n\nThe conclusion **pins the witness to the decomposition**: it asserts both that\n`w` splits and that the reduction holds with the expectation built from *that*\nsplit. A bare `∃ Ew, …` would have been weaker in a way that matters here — a\ndegenerate trace (`tr = 0`, the case `markov_axioms_vacuous_of_weight_zero`\nalready records upstream) satisfies `∃ Ew` for any `Ew` at all, so the\nexistential alone would carry no information about the coset structure. Tying\nthe two conjuncts together is what stops the statement being satisfiable by a\nlucky witness.\n\nThe grounding hypotheses are the genuine mathematical input; the decomposition\nis what lets them cover every `w` rather than only pre-decomposed ones. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.cyclic_two_g_of_tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.cyclic_two_g_of_tower","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L132-L154","doc":"**The reduction.** Ocneanu two-generator cyclicity on the tower, from the\ninduction hypothesis and the Markov reduction ALONE — the other five arguments\nof `MarkovInductive.cyclic_two_g` are discharged above.\n\nStill conditional on `HeckeConditionalExpectation`, which has no instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.towerTrace_mul_eq_of_memB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.towerTrace_mul_eq_of_memB","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L114-L130","doc":"**`hCE`, derived.** For `a` in the level-`n` subalgebra the trace cannot\ntell `a * x` from `a * E x`.\n\nBoth sides evaluate to `trn (y * ε x)` where `a = ι y`: the left by the\nbimodule law, the right because `ι y * ι (ε x) = ι (y * ε x)` and `ε` retracts\n`ι`. This is the only one of the four discharged bricks with mathematical\ncontent — the other three are facts about the image of an algebra map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.epsilon_inclusion_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.epsilon_inclusion_mul","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L100-L112","doc":"**The bimodule law at `z = 1`**: `ε (ι y * x) = y * ε x`.\n\nThis is `bimodule` with the right factor trivialised, and it is the step that\ncarries the weight in `towerTrace_mul_eq_of_memB` below.\n\nThe conditional-expectation instance is bound by NAME rather than left to\ninstance search: `q`, `σn` and `σn1` appear nowhere else in this statement, so\nthey are pinned only by unification against `inst`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.memB_towerE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.memB_towerE","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L96-L98","doc":"`E` lands in the subalgebra — `hElow` (and, with `memBlow := memB`,\n`hlowB` is `id`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.memB_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.memB_one","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L93-L94","doc":"The subalgebra contains `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.memB_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.memB_mul","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L88-L91","doc":"The subalgebra is closed under multiplication — `hmul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.towerTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.towerTrace","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L79-L82","doc":"`towerTrace trn ε` — a level-`n` trace pulled up through the conditional\nexpectation. Defining the level-`(n+1)` trace this way is what makes `hCE`\nderivable rather than assumed; see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.towerE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.towerE","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L75-L77","doc":"`towerE ι ε` — the conditional expectation viewed as an endomorphism of\n`Hn1`, which is the shape `MarkovInductive.cyclic_two_g` expects of `E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.memB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge.memB","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovTowerBridge.lean#L70-L73","doc":"`memB ι x` — \"`x` lies in the level-`n` subalgebra\", i.e. in the image of\nthe tower inclusion. This is the concrete reading of `MarkovInductive`'s\nabstract `memB`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}